The first symbolic attempt exposed a prover limitation: it would not use arithmetic equality under an opaque recursively defined list function. I’m reformulating the postcondition as an accumulator-style mathematical completion function. It still states the contract independently (using factorial/triangular definitions), but its equations align directly with one loop iteration, which is the standard shape for a circular K proof.
